                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/155</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State of a Conversation
                        With the Japanese Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Debuchi</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-09-14">September 14, 1929</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>When the Ambassador called I asked him if there was anything new in the
                    China-Japan situation with regard to extraterritoriality. He told me that China
                    claimed to have annulled the extraterritoriality rights of Japan but that Japan
                    had not admitted it.</p>
            </div>
